<p>The Daily Papers list page does not carry the details of each paper. So Claude Code</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>visits each paper's individual page (WebFetch)</strong> from the list,</li>
    <li>pulls the <strong>abstract</strong> from each page,</li>
    <li>and <strong>organizes everything by category</strong> into a file.</li>
</ul>
<p>At the time of the exercise, a total of 16 papers were organized by category, each with its content, into a single file.</p>

<div class="note">
    <span class="nh">Putting it to use</span>
    Instead of opening papers one by one, it is far faster to pull the relevant papers in wholesale, have the AI do a <strong>first-pass analysis</strong>, and skim the result. This organized file feeds into the "paper showcase site" and the "paper analysis agent" later on.
</div>
